            <ArticleTitle>Extradural spinal cord compression by rheumatoid nodule.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>255-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rheumatoid disease is a systemic disorder affecting multiple organs. It is known to affect the nervous system in a variety of ways, but its presentation with spinal cord compression by a rheumatoid nodule is rare. We report two cases presenting with cord compression by a rheumatoid nodule who underwent surgical decompression with good recovery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
